 protein that is recognized in the host cytoplasm.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>7766</fpage><lpage>7771</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15894622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004790-Birch1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Birch</surname><given-names>PRJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rehmany</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Pritchard</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamoun</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Beynon</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Trafficking arms: Oomycete effectors enter host plant cells.</article-title><source>Trends Microbiol</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16356717</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004790-Morgan1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamoun</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>RXLR effectors of plant pathogenic oomycetes.</article-title><source>Curr Op Microbiol</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>332</fpage><lpage>338</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004790-Whisson1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Whisson</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Boevink</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Moleleki</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Avrova</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><name><surname>Morales</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>A translocation signal for delivery of oomycete effector pro